FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after ferrion-passphrase-wipe.patch and ferrion-key-slots.patch:
- zero the header ring when creating a volume: FileSystem::create_reserved, which redoxfs-mkfs, redoxfs-ar and redoxfs-clone call, writes zeros over all HEADER_RING header blocks before it writes the new header, so a header left by an older volume on the same disk can no longer be picked when the new volume is opened.
- a test creates a volume over one whose ring holds newer headers and opens the new one.

diff --git a/src/filesystem.rs b/src/filesystem.rs
